      {
        "title": {
          "en": "Microsoft Research Introduces ADeLe for AI Performance Prediction and Explanation",
          "zh": "微软研究院推出 ADeLe，预测并解释人工智能性能"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Microsoft researchers, in collaboration with Princeton University and Universitat Politècnica de València, introduced ADeLe to predict and explain AI performance across tasks.",
          "zh": "微软研究人员与普林斯顿大学及瓦伦西亚理工大学合作，推出了 ADeLe，旨在预测和解释人工智能在不同任务上的性能。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "ADeLe is designed to predict AI performance and explain underlying capabilities, addressing limitations of current benchmarks.",
            "Existing AI benchmarks report performance on specific tasks but offer limited insight into the driving capabilities behind that performance.",
            "ADeLe aims to explain AI model failures and reliably predict outcomes on novel tasks."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "ADeLe 旨在预测人工智能性能并解释其潜在能力，以弥补当前基准测试的局限性。",
            "现有的人工智能基准测试报告特定任务的性能，但对驱动其性能的底层能力提供的信息有限。",
            "ADeLe 致力于解释人工智能模型的失败原因并可靠预测其在新任务上的表现。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This initiative could enhance the understanding of how AI models function, enabling more effective diagnosis of performance issues and more accurate forecasting of model behavior on unseen tasks, thereby advancing AI development and deployment.",
          "zh": "这一举措可能增强对人工智能模型工作原理的理解，从而更有效地诊断性能问题，并更准确地预测模型在未知任务上的行为，进而推动人工智能的开发和部署。"
        },
        "source": "Microsoft Research",
        "link": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/adele-predicting-and-explaining-ai-performance-across-tasks/"
      }
    ],
